Here's a JavaScript code snippet that uses the `mousedown`, `mousemove`, and `mouseup` events to programmatically click on an element and drag it 5px to the right. This example assumes that the element has an ID of `draggableElement`.

```javascript
// Get the draggable element
const draggableElement = document.getElementById('draggableElement');

// Add event listeners for mousedown, mousemove, and mouseup
let isDragging = false;
let offsetX;

draggableElement.addEventListener('mousedown', (e) => {
  isDragging = true;
  offsetX = e.clientX - draggableElement.getBoundingClientRect().left;
});

document.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {
  if (isDragging) {
    const newX = e.clientX - offsetX;
    draggableElement.style.left = `${newX}px`;
  }
});

document.addEventListener('mouseup', () => {
  isDragging = false;
});

// To drag the element 5px to the right programmatically, you can use the following code:
function dragElementToRight() {
  const currentLeft = parseInt(getComputedStyle(draggableElement).left) || 0;
  draggableElement.style.left = `${currentLeft + 5}px`;
}

// Call the function to drag the element 5px to the right
dragElementToRight();
```

