    margin-top: 20px;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    position: relative;
}

.speaker-row {
    height: 20px;
    position: relative;
}

.speaker-segment {
    position: absolute;
    height: 100%;
    background-color: #ff6347; /* Tomato color for active speaking */
}
```

### JavaScript
Finally, use JavaScript to dynamically create the speaker timeline based on the video duration and speaker data.

```javascript
// script.js
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const video = document.getElementById('conferenceVideo');
    const timeline = document.getElementById('speakerTimeline');

    // Sample speaker data (start time, end time) in seconds
    const speakers = [
        { name: 'Speaker 1', segments: [{ start: 10, end: 30 }, { start: 60, end: 90 }] },
        { name: 'Speaker 2', segments: [{ start: 35, end: 55 }, { start: 100, end: 120 }] },
        // Add more speakers as needed
    ];

    video.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', () => {
        const duration = video.duration;
        const timelineWidth = timeline.offsetWidth;

        speakers.forEach(speaker => {
            const row = document.createElement('div');
            row.classList.add('speaker-row');
            row.setAttribute('data-speaker', speaker.name);

            speaker.segments.forEach(segment => {
                const segmentElement = document.createElement('div');
                segmentElement.classList.add('speaker-segment');
                segmentElement.style.left = `${(segment.start / duration) * 100}%`;
                segmentElement.style.width = `${((segment.end - segment.start) / duration) * 100}%`;
                row.appendChild(segmentElement);
            });

            timeline.appendChild(row);
        });
    });
});
```

### Explanation
1. **HTML**: The structure includes a video element and a container for the speaker timeline.
2. **CSS**: Styles ensure the timeline width matches the video width and positions the speaker segments correctly.
3. **JavaScript**:
   - Waits for the video metadata to load to get the video duration.
   - Dynamically creates rows for each speaker and segments for each speaking interval.
   - Positions and sizes the segments based on the video duration and timeline width.

This setup ensures that the speaker timeline is always the same width as the video and dynamically updates based on the video's metadata and speaker data.

