I apologize for the confusion. In the previous example, I used the built-in `gzcompress` and `gzuncompress` functions, which are part of the PHP standard library. Here's an updated version of the script that uses a custom compression algorithm based on Huffman coding, without relying on any external dependencies or built-in compression functions.

This example uses a simple implementation of Huffman coding, which is not as efficient as more advanced algorithms like DEFLATE (used in gzip), but it demonstrates the concept of custom compression in PHP.

```php
<?php

// Populate the array
$userData = [
    ['id' => 1, 'name' => 'John Doe', 'email' => 'john@example.com'],
    ['id' => 2, 'name' => 'Jane Smith', 'email' => 'jane@example.com'],
    ['id' => 3, 'name' => 'Mike Johnson', 'email' => 'mike@example.com'],
];

// Serialize the array
$serializedData = serialize($userData);

// Compress the serialized data using Huffman coding
function huffmanCompress($data) {
    $frequencies = array_count_values(str_split($data));
    $nodes = [];

    foreach ($frequencies as $char => $freq) {
        $nodes[] = ['char' => $char, 'freq' => $freq, 'left' => null, 'right' => null];
    }

    usort($nodes, function ($a, $b) {
        return $a['freq'] - $b['freq'];
    });

    while (count($nodes) > 1) {
        $left = array_shift($nodes);
        $right = array_shift($nodes);
        $nodes[] = ['char' => null, 'freq' => $left['freq'] + $right['freq'], 'left' => $left, 'right' => $right];
        usort($nodes, function ($a, $b) {
            return $a['freq'] - $b['freq'];
        });
    }

    $tree = $nodes[0];
    $codes = [];

    function buildCodes($node, $code = '') {
        global $codes;

        if ($node['char'] !== null) {
            $codes[$node['char']] = $code;
        } else {
            buildCodes($node['left'], $code . '0');
            buildCodes($node['right'], $code . '1');
        }
    }

    buildCodes($tree);

    $compressed = '';

    foreach (str_split($data) as $char) {
        $compressed .= $codes[$char];
    }

    return $compressed . '|' . serialize($tree);
}

$compressedData = huffmanCompress($serializedData);

// Save the compressed data to a file
file_put_contents('data.txt.huff', $compressedData);

echo "Data saved to data.txt.huff\n";

// To read, decompress, and unserialize the data from the file
function huffmanDecompress($data) {
    list($compressed, $tree) = explode('|', $data, 2);
    $tree = unserialize($tree);

    $decompressed = '';
    $currentNode = $tree;

    for ($i = 0; $i < strlen($compressed); $i++) {
        if ($compressed[$i] === '0') {
            $currentNode = $currentNode['left'];
        } else {
            $currentNode = $currentNode['right'];
        }

        if ($currentNode['char'] !== null) {
            $decompressed .= $currentNode['char'];
            $currentNode = $tree;
        }
    }

    return $decompressed;
}

$decompressedData = huffmanDecompress(file_get_contents('data.txt.huff'));

if ($decompressedData !== false) {
    // Unserialize the decompressed data
    $unserializedData = unserialize($decompressedData);

    if ($unserializedData !== false) {
        // Print the unserialized data
        print_r($unserializedData);
    } else {
        echo "Error unserializing data\n";
    }
} else {
    echo "Error decompressing data\n";
}

?>
```

