We will build an iOS, Android and Web app for discovering, rating and tracking climbing and boulder crags around the world. We will do so by leveraging the following graphql api https://api.openbeta.io/. The api will not be directly used in the app, instead it is synced via a Firebase Function into our own schema into our Firestore.
Users will be able to discover climbing areas (crags) around the world by using various filters and search terms like difficultiy range (grades), tags (sunny, child friendly, 5min ascent, and so on), location, accesability via public transport, etc.
They will also be able to discover climbing areas using an interactive customized mapbox with open street map.
The app will use a custom design made with nativewind and the universal design system (https://github.com/showtime-xyz/showtime-frontend/tree/staging/packages/design-system). Styled components should be used and created at the top of the page with inline tailwind/nativewind syling. 

The main goal of the app is to bring the users (climbers) to contribute more detailed beta (data like tags, descriptions, routes, ratings, even new areas, etc.) about the climbing areas because the data from obenbeta is very basic and contains limited information. This should be done in a fun way for the user and the octalysis framework (https://yukaichou.com/gamification-examples/octalysis-complete-gamification-framework/) and other gamification thechniques should be used to motivate the users to contribute.The main game loop is a cycle of discovery -> contribution -> enbaling a richer discovery.
Users should also be able to track their climbed routes (ticks) and data associated with it (health, smartwatch).
In the long term the app should become THE app to find and discover new climbing areas and to plan the next climbing tripp. Including auxilarry information like weather, exposure, ascent, public or personal transport (car), offline access, topos (contributed by users), and much more.
The protection of the nature and envionment also plays an important role in climbing and local restrictions and ethical rules must be clearly visible in the app. THe users should also learn in a playful way about the local flora and fauna and how to preserve it.
