```cpp
#include <cmath>

float wrapTo2Pi(float angle) {
    angle = fmod(angle, 2 * M_PI);  // wrap to [-2PI, 2PI]
    if (angle < 0) {
        angle += 2 * M_PI;  // move to [0, 2PI]
    }
    return angle;
}
```

This function uses the `fmod` function from the `cmath` library to find the remainder of the division of the input angle by 2PI, which wraps the angle to the range [-2PI, 2PI]. If the result is negative, it adds 2PI to move it to the range [0, 2PI].

Please note that `M_PI` is a constant defined in `cmath` that represents the value of PI. If your compiler does not support `M_PI`, you can define it yourself as follows:

