1. A `chatRooms` object to store chat rooms and their respective clients.
2. A `join room` event to allow clients to join a chat room.
3. A `leave room` event to allow clients to leave a chat room.
4. A `store message` event to store chat messages in the socket's data object.
5. A `room messages` event to send all previous messages in the room to the new client when they join.

Now, clients can join and leave chat rooms, and chat messages will be sent to all clients in the same room.

